# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.local — local dev only. NEVER commit .env.local.
# Vercel project env holds the production values; copy them down for local
# dev (Vercel CLI: `vercel env pull .env.local`).
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Canonical assembl-prod Supabase project (project ref: wurwcrgxjjwqdaxqceey,
# Sydney region). Confirmed by Kate 2026-05-09 — the project name carries the
# "Lovable" lineage but it IS the live assembl-prod where Vercel auth, edge
# functions, and migrations all run today.
# Get these values from Supabase Studio → Project Settings → API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://wurwcrgxjjwqdaxqceey.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# Optional — founder gate cookie passphrase for /dashboard/vessel-studio.
# Out of scope for the Supabase auth wiring.
# FOUNDER_GATE_SECRET=""

# ── Hui meeting agent ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Audio transcription provider (Deepgram). Without this key, Hui's
# upload/record tabs show "coming online soon" and the paste-transcript
# path stays fully live. LLM + evidence-pack rendering reuse the existing
# Supabase edge functions (no extra key needed).
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=""
# Force-disable transcription even if a key is present (rollout flag).
HUI_TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER_CONFIGURED=""

# ── HAPAI lead capture → Brevo mailing list ───────────────────────
# When a visitor adds their email at a HAPAI tool's gating wall, the lead is
# subscribed to the single assembl mailing list in Brevo (the ESP already
# running this stack — the notify leg uses it too). Both vars must be set or the
# Brevo leg is a silent no-op — leads still land in Supabase (hapai_leads /
# lead_inquiries) and the assembl inbox regardless. NOTE: Brevo's "Authorised
# IPs" setting must allow serverless egress (or be off) for this leg to land.
BREVO_API_KEY=""
BREVO_LIST_ID=""

# ── Pipeline health monitoring (health-check-cron edge function + /admin/health) ──
# Shared secret used to (a) invoke the health-check-cron function manually
# (x-api-key header or Bearer) and (b) gate the /admin/health dashboard
# (?key=...). The 5-minute pg_cron schedule invokes it with the service-role
# key, so this is only needed for manual runs + the dashboard.
HEALTH_CHECK_API_KEY=""
# POST target for failure alerts (Slack/Discord/generic webhook). This is the
# IP-block-resilient channel: if Brevo blocks our IP, email alerts stop but the
# webhook still fires. Leave empty to disable the webhook leg.
HEALTH_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=""
